<description>
Transform each 9x9 panel by mirroring across its center guide line or filling all four block slots from its lone exemplar.

Input structure
The grid is made of 9x9 panels separated by one-cell-wide grid lines. Each
panel has four monochrome 3x3 slots at the quadrant positions, with either a
full non-background center row, a full non-background center column, or no
guide line.

Rule
A panel with a full center column is reflected left-to-right, and a panel
with a full center row is reflected top-to-bottom. A panel with no guide line
has exactly one slot color that appears once and one slot color that appears
three times; recolor all four slots to the once-occurring slot color.

Key insight
The center guide line encodes the mirror axis, while panels without a guide
line are completed by copying the structurally unique slot color.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "9x9 panel lattice; each panel has four monochrome 3x3 quadrant slots and optionally a full center-row or center-column guide line",
  "transform": "reflect each guided panel across its guide line; for each unguided panel, recolor all four slots to the slot color that appears only once"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: NR x NC panels of 9x9, separated by 1-cell-wide lines; total = (NR*10-1) x (NC*10-1)
  panel_grid: NR=1-3, NC=1-3 (observed range 1x1 to 3x3); NR*NC >= 1
  separator: single non-0 non-4 color filling all inter-panel rows/cols uniformly; omitted when NR=NC=1
  background: always 0
  panel_structure: |
    Each 9x9 panel has: row/col 0 and 8 are bg border; row/col 4 is center cross.
    Four 3x3 monochrome slots at quadrant positions (rows 1-3,5-7 x cols 1-3,5-7).
  panel_types:
    col_axis: center column (col 4) filled with color 4; all 4 slots non-bg; at least 2 distinct slot colors
    row_axis: center row (row 4) filled with color 4; all 4 slots non-bg; at least 2 distinct slot colors
    no_guide: center cross all bg; exactly 3 slots color-1, 1 slot a unique color != 0 and != 1
  panel_type_mix: each grid has at least 1 panel; any combination of types allowed
  guide_color: always 4
  slot_colors: non-0; guided panels use any non-0 colors (may include 1 or sep color); no_guide unique color is any color in 2-9
  transform:
    col_axis: flip panel left-right (swaps TL<->TR, BL<->BR slots)
    row_axis: flip panel top-bottom (swaps TL<->BL, TR<->BR slots)
    no_guide: recolor all 4 slots to the unique (non-1) slot color

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (panels are independent; no cross-panel constraints)
  steps:
    1. Pick NR, NC in 1-3 each. Pick separator color from {2-9} minus {4}.
    2. For each panel position, choose type (col_axis, row_axis, or no_guide).
    3. For no_guide panels, pick unique-slot position (TL/TR/BL/BR) and a color in 2-9 excluding 1.
       Fill 3 slots with color 1, 1 slot with the unique color.
    4. For guided panels, pick 4 non-0 slot colors (may repeat, may include 1/sep color).
       Place guide line (color 4) on center col (col_axis) or center row (row_axis).
    5. Assemble 9x9 panels into grid with separator lines between them.
  output_derivation: apply transform per panel type (flip or fill) -- trivially deterministic.
